notes: a notes service over SQLite, and its client

usage: notes <command> [arguments] [options]

server commands:
  serve                      serve the HTTP JSON API on --addr until Ctrl-C
  replay                     answer raw HTTP/1.1 requests from standard input on standard output
  import FILE                add the notes of a JSON array file in one transaction
  export                     print every note as a JSON array
  backup                     copy every note of --db into --to
  version                    print the program's and sqlite's versions

client commands, sent to the server at --addr:
  health                     ask whether the server is up
  version                    the server's sqlite version and normalizer
  add TITLE [BODY] [TAG...]  create a note
  get ID                     show one note
  list [q=T] [tag=T] [limit=N] [offset=N]
  search TEXT                notes whose title or body contains TEXT, ignoring case and spacing
  edit ID FIELD=VALUE...     change title, body or tags (tags=a,b; tags= clears them)
  rm ID                      delete a note
  stats                      counts over every note
  raw METHOD PATH [BODY]     send any request and print the reply as it came
  batch                      run the client commands of standard input, one a line
  load                       post --requests notes from each of --clients tasks at once

Options:
  --help            Print this help and exit
  --db <str>        The database file (serve, replay, import, export, backup, and client commands with --embed)
  --addr <str>      The address to serve on, or the server to reach, as host:port (default 127.0.0.1:8080)
  --limit <int>     The largest request body in bytes (default 1048576)
  --log <str>       Write the request log to this file, replacing it, instead of printing it at exit
  --level <str>     The least request log level: debug, info, warn or error (default info)
  --quiet           Print no request log
  --clients <int>   Concurrent clients (load, default 4)
  --requests <int>  New notes each client sends (load, default 25)
  --to <str>        The database to copy into (backup)
  --embed           Serve --db on --addr inside this process for the client commands, batch and load
Arguments:
  <args>...         The command and its arguments
